- TLSv1.2 in order to validate ownership of the certificate from the server ---> Client creates Pre-Master-Secret and encrypts it with the public key of the server. 
                                                                                 The only who can decrypt it is the server itself with the private key. Server notifies with encrypted Verification about having session keys which postulates right ownership of certificate. (RSA Variante)

                                                                                 Wie berechne ich aus den Pre-Master-Secret die Session keys ?



